title: Payers › Rules › Read the rules
route: /payers/summit?tab=rules
intro: Four rule cards for one payer, each a few plain lines, with the agents that use them and the date they were last confirmed. The saved lines are what New case reads for this payer; editing them is the next diagram. In the product, each field would carry a source and a confidence (published, payer-confirmed, observed, staff-reported, unconfirmed).
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click the 'Rules' tab"
screen tab "Rules tab\nBanner if edits wait, four cards in two columns, a note"
decision dU "Edits saved but not yet\napplied to open drafts?"
toast bU "'1 edit applies to new drafts only'\nwith 'Update 2 drafts'\nSent requests keep what they were sent with"
goto gU "Continues in: Payers › Edits waiting › Update drafts"

group gC "Each card"
  screen c1 "Submission windows\nNotice within 24 hours of admission (72 for Harborview, by phone for Evergreen, by fax for Lakeshore)\nRecertification filed 72 hours before the unit limit\nA continued-stay review every 7 days after the first 7"
  screen c2 "Backdating\nDiffers by payer: Summit and Cardinal do not backdate,\nBeacon backdates within 2 business days,\nEvergreen up to 3 days with a call log, Lakeshore to the fax receipt date"
  screen c3 "No authorization needed\nIndividual therapy, Medication management,\nInitial assessment, Crisis stabilization first 24 hours\n(Evergreen has no crisis line). Shown with green ticks"
  screen c4 "Peer-to-peer and appeals\nSummit: peer-to-peer call within 3 business days (Cardinal 2),\nwritten appeal within 60 days, expedited 72 hours,\nthen external review (Evergreen: state hearing)"
endgroup

process ub "Foot of each card\n'Used by Cadence and Navigator · confirmed 10/12'"
process who "Used by\nWindows: Cadence, Navigator\nBackdating: Cadence, Scrubber\nNo authorization needed: Verify, Criteria\nPeer-to-peer and appeals: Advocate, Cadence"
process cf "'Confirmed' is a date\nEvergreen shows 10/09, the others 10/12\nIt moves to today when a rule is edited"
toast note "'Rules are learned from past decisions and confirmed against\nSummit's published policy. New drafts use a saved edit at once.\nSent requests keep what they were sent with.\nClick Update drafts to redraft open ones.'"
process noeff "New case reads the saved lines for the payer\nand level of care of each draft\nSee the New case diagrams for what it checks"
click ce "Click 'Edit' on a card\n(the button is named 'Edit Backdating' and so on)"
goto gE "Continues in: Payers › Rules › Edit a rule"
goto gF "Continues in: Payers › Configuration feeds the rest of the app"

s1 --> tab --> dU
dU -->|Yes| bU --> gU
dU -->|No| c1
bU --> c1
c1 --> c2 --> c3 --> c4
c1 --> ub --> who --> cf
c4 --> note
c4 --> ce --> gE
note -.-> noeff
noeff -.-> gF
